echnicians new images from satellites, and even helping prospectors locate oil from enhanced seismic readings--all at a speed some 200 times faster than previous computer programs.","evidence":"documented","universe":"pixar","aliases":["Pixar"],"wikipedia_url":null,"image_url":null,"image_source":null,"image_credit":null,"image_license":null,"image_usage":null,"image_alt":null},"connections":[{"id":"b42faed5-a08f-42ca-8ed6-ae445e615eba","relationship":"part_of","title":"Part of","explanation":"Part of","strength":"0.9000","discovery_score":"0.8500","direction":"incoming","from_entity_id":"52468fbd-fb35-4ad1-9846-7e7eb3a6916b","to_entity_id":"e35672e2-450d-46d3-a4d4-d309da368a51","entity_id":"52468fbd-fb35-4ad1-9846-7e7eb3a6916b","slug":"planes","name":"Planes","type":"work","short_description":"Planes is the first film in the Planes franchise. It was produced by DisneyToon Studios and takes place in the Cars universe, although Pixar was not involved in its production. It was theatrically released on August 9,…","evidence":"fiction","image_url":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/pixar/images/3/3f/D82FE1DA-6D94-4CD2-92B8-43B92EFD1614.jpeg/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/180?cb=20181127153106","path":"/pixar/planes","kind":"work","type_label":"Work"}],"rabbit_holes":[],"copyright":{"theme":"pixar","title":"Pixar is not owned by Ton-o-Lore.","body":"Pixar, related names, marks, and materials are the property of Pixar / Disney / respective rights holders. Ton-o-Lore is an independent educational encyclopedia project and is not affiliated with or endorsed by those rights holders. Identification marks, when shown, are low-resolution images used under a fair-use rationale for commentary and identification only — not free or redistributable artwork."},"subject":{"id":"pixar","name":"Pixar","theme":"pixar","path":"/pixar","logo":null,"categories":["western-animation"]}}